Fillets: a walked blend whose contour goes on round a corner rounded more
sharply than the ball walks on along the corner's face (mitcad#308).

0160 made StartSol refuse a face beyond a tangent edge that bends towards
the ball more sharply than the ball (ballCannotTouch), to bridge the
rounded rim of a hole or cut-out of the contact's face. That also refused
a face the contour itself runs along: a box whose vertical edges are
rounded with 2, its bottom chamfered round the box, then the edge between
the chamfer and a side face rounded with 5 (the contour goes on round the
corners, between the chamfer's cone and the corner's cylinder). There the
spine turns with the face, the sections touch it, and the walk went on
onto it before 0160; after, no face continued the contact, the bridge over
a gap found none, and the fillet failed (Chaining is impossible).

- StartSol: a face beyond that borders an edge of the spine (faceAlongSpine)
  continues the contact's face whatever its curvature along the spine; the
  test of 0160 applies to other faces only.
